  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile this change correctly formats the JSON output for non-ASCII characters, using `print()` for debugging or logging in a library is not a good practice. It writes directly to `stdout`, which can clutter the output of applications using this library and cannot be configured (e.g., redirected to a file or silenced based on severity).\n\nIt's highly recommended to use Python's standard `logging` module instead. This allows for flexible configuration of log levels and outputs. Based on the code's purpose, a `DEBUG` level log seems appropriate here.\n\nTo follow the project's convention (as seen in files like `verl/experimental/agent_loop/tool_parser.py`), you should add the following at the top of the file:\n```python\nimport logging\nimport os\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__file__)\nlogger.setLevel(os.getenv(\"VERL_LOGGING_LEVEL\", \"WARN\"))\n```\nThen, you can replace the `print()` call with the suggested code.\n\n```suggestion\n        logger.debug(json.dumps(self.tool_schema.model_dump(exclude_unset=True, exclude_none=True), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-01-07T03:46:27Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ def __init__(self, config: dict, tool_schema: OpenAIFunctionToolSchema):\n         self.tool_schema = tool_schema or self.get_openai_tool_schema()\n         assert self.tool_schema is not None, \"Tool schema is not set!\"\n         self.name = self.tool_schema.function.name\n-        print(json.dumps(self.tool_schema.model_dump(exclude_unset=True, exclude_none=True), indent=2))\n+        print(json.dumps(self.tool_schema.model_dump(exclude_unset=True, exclude_none=True), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))",
